  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description and Provenance
    
    The Radiant Aurora-harp stands as tall as a penguin's flipper-span. Its frame is carved from a single piece of eternal ice — deep crystal drawn from Light Ingjeizhi, the aurora-crystal spire anchoring the Promenade Ward — and catches light from within, casting prismatic shadows that move independent of any external source. The forty-seven strings are aurora-glass filaments drawn from the spire's own veins, nearly invisible until struck. One string has hung slack for three seasons, resonating at a register only crystal lattice carries. No one living remembers who first played it, or when it was made. The provenance connecting the harp to Light Ingjeizhi's deep crystal is well attested in the archive-ice, though the penguins who play it have largely forgotten it.
    
    ## Discovery and Custody
    
    The harp was found sealed in Light Ingjeizhi's deepest archive during the early Frozen Peace by an unnamed traveler who claimed it as their own and, within a rotation, Walked into the sea. The Pinnacle, the breakaway Aurora Stack faction led by Plunge-Caller Oeichowei, took possession afterward. Whether this constituted custodianship or opportunism is a question no one has formally raised, which is itself an answer of sorts. The Pinnacle later returned the harp to Light Ingjeizhi's central alcove for the mandated hearings Oeichowei required before swearing the coded greeting. It remains under Pinnacle control, though Qingfu'spire has demanded its return — a dispute that shows no sign of resolution.
    
    ## Acoustic Properties
    
    The harp's frequencies correspond to events preserved in ice-memory with uncomfortable precision. One frequency, which the old mystics called *the unworthy wind*, matches the pitch of the aurora at its northward swing during the Long Dark's deepest point. Another has been matched to the sound produced when three orca pods struck the Berg's thermal vents simultaneously during the Shelf Crushing Offense — the pitch of fire-cores beginning to dim. The harp resonates unprompted, humming without player or touch. Those nearby flinch. This is consistent across accounts.
    
    ## The Faceless Xi
    
    The faceless Xi — a former Aurora Stack mystic exiled for smuggling fire-cores in violation of the Flipper Accord — heard the harp twice. The first hearing produced *the unworthy wind* and years of what the sources call blood-salt sleeplessness. The second time, the harp activated without being touched and stripped fire-core corruption from Xi's body, performing what can only be described as a claiming. No custodial body authorized this. The Pinnacle has not formally adjudicated whether what occurred constitutes a hearing or a blessing. The distinction matters politically; the harp does not appear to share the concern.
    
    ## The Three Fracture-Lines
    
    The ice frame bears three sealed but unhealed cracks:
    
    | Fracture | Source | Activation Response |
    |---|---|---|
    | First | The Mbra∴silentiu | Glows amber |
    | Second | Ice-Crowned Shexuwohua's seizure during the succession crisis Of The First Shelf | Pulses white |
    | Third | The Breach (ice-screamed) | Remains dark |
    
    During activation, each scar responds independently. The harp carries its political history in its wounds and, by all accounts, chooses which to display. I note only that an artifact which remembers three wars in its body and selects which scars to show is doing something more complex than resonating.
