  annotation "note_1771580951629_1", anchor: "three orca pods struck the Berg's thermal vents simultaneously during the Shelf Crushing Offense", text: "Thermal vents supply fire-cores. Sources from the first week call the orca commander pod-lieutenant — a defensive rank. Deep ice at stratum 4 preserves penguin encroachment on adjacent hunting grounds the preceding season. If the Offense was retaliatory, the harp is not resonating with an attack. It is resonating with a consequence.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771580951629_2", anchor: "Remains dark", text: "The Breach was the most recent and most destructive of the three. The older wounds respond. This one does not. I have spent my career distinguishing silence from absence in damaged ice-memory — silence is the ice choosing not to speak; absence is what remains when the memory has been consumed. A sealed but unhealed crack that produces no light when activated warrants direct examination. The Pinnacle will not permit it. I requested access eleven days ago. No reply. Not a refusal — simply nothing, which is its own variety of dark.", type: :commentary, display: :full
